.$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s),\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86e56d87-8f7f-5aac-9c51-653244b0266e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281522 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{s}$ is $s\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,2).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{3}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/80/808abeaa59d7bcea3b24e741fde5296791de32b4170d60f05f2a5af203c20ba2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in [0,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "669d7279-38d4-5150-94a0-6a97a679c0f2